{"text": "From: Bronwyn Castellanos <bronwyn@copperlineoutfitters.example>\nTo: Ravi Subramanian <ravi@copperlineoutfitters.example>\nDate: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 18:07:44 -0600\nSubject: everything you need while I'm out (7/20-8/7) - PLEASE DELETE AFTER READING\n\nRavi,\n\nI know, I know, I shouldn't put all this in one email. But you asked for one\nplace to look, so here it is. Delete it when I'm back.\n\nPAYMENTS DUE WHILE I'M GONE\n\n1) Sawtooth Freight Lines, Inc. -- invoice SFL-208841, $4,318.90, due July 24, Net 30.\n   Pay by ACH from the bank portal. They are already set up as a payee but if\n   it asks again: routing 064808675, account 3300447182. Their Form W-9 is in\n   the vendor folder.\n\n2) Maier Textil GmbH & Co. KG -- the wool order. EUR 11,240.00 by international\n   wire, must arrive by July 31 or Ingeborg will not ship before the fall\n   catalog. Details exactly as on her pro-forma:\n       Beneficiary: Maier Textil GmbH & Co. KG\n       IBAN: DE12 9249 1078 0589 9210 51\n       BIC: MAIEDEM1XXX\n       Reference: PF-7741\n   The bank charges $45 per wire. If the portal balks at the amount, call\n   Tasha Greenleaf at First Teton Bank & Trust, (208) 555-0166. She knows us. She will\n   ask for the callback PIN, which is 4471.\n\n3) The software subscriptions bill to the company card, the one ending 2830.\n   If anything declines, the full number is 6011 2427 4797 0830, exp 03/28, CVV 529.\n   Do NOT give that to anyone over the phone.\n\nBANK PORTAL\n   https://business.firstteton.example/login\n   user: copperline_ap\n   pass: Huckleberry!Trail88\n   2FA codes go to my cell, so text me (208-555-0134) BEFORE you log in and I\n   will send the code. I'll have service most days.\n\nQuickBooks runs on the back-office PC. Windows login is coadmin / Winter2026$.\n(Yes, Mike keeps telling me to change it.)\n\nIT STUFF, since Mike O'Dell of O'Dell Networks is also away the week of the 27th:\n   - If the internet drops, power-cycle the router in the stock room. Its admin\n     page is 192.168.10.1. Static IP from the ISP is 203.0.113.88 -- Mike says\n     the card terminal needs that.\n   - Label printer by the packing bench keeps falling off the network. It is\n     the one with MAC 00:1B:44:11:3A:B7, serial ZT41-2291-00817. Turn it off and on.\n   - Remote support, only if desperate: mike@odellnetworks.example or 208.555.0191.\n\nPEOPLE THINGS (between us)\n   - Tasha is not just our banker, she is my sister-in-law, so be nice.\n   - If Mr. Subramanian senior calls about the lease, tell your dad I will\n     ring him the week I'm back. The deposit he fronted us, $18,000, is on\n     the books as a loan, not equity. We agreed that at Christmas.\n   - I'm out for my knee replacement, not a vacation, whatever the PTO\n     calendar says. Please keep that to yourself.\n\nThank you thank you.\nB.\n\n--\nBronwyn Castellanos\nOperations, Copperline Outfitters Co.\n118 N. Main St., Driggs, ID 83422", "kind": "Email", "detail": "469 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Bronwyn Castellanos", "Ravi Subramanian", "Tasha Greenleaf", "Mike", "Mike O'Dell", "Tasha", "Mr. Subramanian senior"], "companies": ["Copperline Outfitters", "Sawtooth Freight Lines, Inc.", "Maier Textil GmbH & Co. KG", "First Teton Bank & Trust", "O'Dell Networks", "Copperline Outfitters Co."]}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "importMs": 0.7000000029802322, "modelMs": 30154.5, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "phone", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "street", "zip", "postal_ca", "places", "names"], "detections": [{"start": 6, "end": 25, "text": "Bronwyn Castellanos", "kind": "person", "source": "model", "canonical": "Bronwyn Castellanos"}, {"start": 27, "end": 63, "text": "bronwyn@copperlineoutfitters.example", "kind": "email", "source": "pattern", "canonical": "bronwyn@copperlineoutfitters.example"}, {"st